{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:56:44.468Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d4e09f202aeeaf59f9a43790e8b32713528e43a5e4e20f4c65e057dff9ee22c0","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files: four North digests and two Central ones. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't texting bay assignments to drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 for the 04:00 shift. Support patched it at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift went through fine. The note also asked for the kiosk logs to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The note isn't dated, so I can't tell you when it was raised or where it stands now.\n\nThings I left out:\n• The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers.\n• The Central notes have #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company, which isn't a customer.\n\nMoss hasn't posted anything about this in #general or #help-it-ops."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
